view structure · wall_panel
marks: ● mutable state (← who changes it) · !n invariant n · ? gap: the description does not say · ∅ declared absence: none, on purpose · ⚠ warning · ⏱ timeout · ⟳ period

structure (level 0 uses the ones below)
level 0:
deploy.sh · shell script !12
  → runs in dev workstation; writes pages, server host, panel-server
mosquitto · process
  → listens on 127.0.0.1:1883; runs in server host
level 1:
panel-server · process !1,2,6-10,12,13
  runs in systemd panel-server.service
  config.json · configuration (immutable)
  Store · key-value
  screen cache · map ● ← changed by accept device
  alert queue · queue
  navigation stack · stack ● ← changed by accept device
  SOC alert · state ● ← changed by monitor
  accept device · thread
  clock · thread ⟳60 s
  control · thread
  monitor · thread
  mqtt · thread
  session ping · thread ⟳5 s
  weather · thread ⟳1800 s
  → connects to 127.0.0.1:1883, 0.0.0.0:9222; launches curl; listens on server:8993, server:9000; reads pages; renders buffer L8 1072x1448; runs in server host; sends paneld; uses chrome-headless-shell
level 2:
chrome-headless-shell · process !4
  runs in systemd, Nice 19
  → listens on 0.0.0.0:9222; runs in server host
curl · process
  → reads open-meteo; runs in server host
pages · directory
  dark theme · page
  home.html · page
  launcher.html · page
paneld · process !3,5,11
  runs in init session
  touch targets · list
  connection · state ● ← changed by paneld
  screen ownership · state ● ← changed by paneld
  reconnect backoff · timer ⟳1 s to 60 s
  → connects to server:8993; runs in panel device; sends panel-server

externals
0.0.0.0:9222 · devtools endpoint ?
127.0.0.1:1883 · mqtt endpoint ?
buffer L8 1072x1448 · device
dev workstation · machine
open-meteo · web service
panel device · machine
server host · machine
server:8993 · tcp endpoint ∅
server:9000 · http endpoint ?

state machines
machine SOC alert (in panel-server): states normal (initial), alert
  normal → alert: monitor
  alert → normal: monitor
machine connection (in paneld): states waiting backoff, disconnected (initial), connected
  waiting backoff → disconnected: paneld
  disconnected → connected: paneld
  connected → waiting backoff: paneld
machine screen ownership (in paneld): states external app, session (initial)
  external app → session: paneld
  session → external app: paneld

threads
accept device: changes navigation stack, screen cache; consumes Store, alert queue
clock ⟳60 s: fills Store
control: fills alert queue
monitor: consumes Store; fills alert queue; moves SOC alert
mqtt: connects to 127.0.0.1:1883; fills Store; subscribes to home/energy/#, home/sensor/data, home/weather/#
session ping ⟳5 s
weather ⟳1800 s: fills Store; launches curl
shared Store · key-value store: accept device consumes, mqtt fills, weather fills, clock fills, monitor consumes
shared alert queue · queue: control fills, accept device consumes, monitor fills

roles (what the primitives presuppose)
config.json · configuration: source=panel-server; validation=panel-server
0.0.0.0:9222 · devtools endpoint: address=chrome-headless-shell; authentication=?
server:9000 · http endpoint: address=panel-server; authentication=?
127.0.0.1:1883 · mqtt endpoint: address=mosquitto; authentication=?
server:8993 · tcp endpoint: address=panel-server; authentication=∅
Store · key-value store: key=data key
screen cache · map: key=page
alert queue · queue: capacity=bounded
reconnect backoff · timer: period=1 s to 60 s

invariants and rules
!1 If the value "rectangle" is monochrome, the process "panel-server" uses the value "A2".
!2 If the stack "navigation stack" changes, the process "panel-server" uses the value "GC16".
!3 If the connection "session" closes, the process "paneld" connects to the tcp endpoint "server:8993".
!4 When the process "chrome-headless-shell" launches, the process "chrome-headless-shell" removes the value "SingletonLock".
!5 If the connection "session" times out, the process "paneld" launches the process "udhcpc".
!6 If the devtools endpoint "0.0.0.0:9222" times out, the process "panel-server" falls back to the function "native render".
!7 If the thread "mqtt" times out, the thread "monitor" publishes the alert "dead source" to the queue "alert queue".
!8 If the value "home.soc" is less than 30, the thread "monitor" publishes the alert "low SOC" to the queue "alert queue".
!9 If the value "home.soc" is greater than 35, the thread "monitor" removes the alert "low SOC" from the queue "alert queue".
!10 If the counter "consecutive A2 per region" is at least 8, the process "panel-server" dispatches the event "ghosting cleanup".
!11 The process "paneld" does not call the function "FB_WAIT_UPDATE".
!12 The shell script "deploy.sh" does not overwrite the configuration "config.json".
!13 The process "panel-server" does not change the value "physical screen edge".

gaps (the description does not say), warnings and absences (none, on purpose)
? devtools endpoint “0.0.0.0:9222”: missing authentication
? http endpoint “server:9000”: missing authentication
? mqtt endpoint “127.0.0.1:1883”: missing authentication
∅ tcp endpoint “server:8993”: no authentication, on purpose
